  rung 0  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma diag)   logL = -3774.2845076500

=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=4, q=0)   logL =   -1174.7313188790
  univariate 2 (p=4, q=0)   logL =   -1281.9639206847
  univariate 3 (p=4, q=0)   logL =   -1317.5892680863
                                 sum  =   -3774.2845076500
                                 joint=   -3774.2845076500
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is -3774.2845076500)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -5.002e-12   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   VERIFIED
  rung 1  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma free)   logL = -3484.6985712626
